# Copy this file to .env and replace the placeholder values.
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way: every deploy script begins
# `export $(cat .env | xargs)`, so three of the five values below are live
# credentials. A key committed to a public repository has to be rotated, not
# deleted.
#
# The functions deploy from a laptop rather than from CI. deploy-functions.yml
# exists but guards on GH_FUNCTIONS_PROJECT_ID, GH_FUNCTIONS_WIF_PROVIDER and
# GH_FUNCTIONS_DEPLOYER_SA, none of which are set, so it skips its deploy job
# and reports why. Until those exist, `npm run deploy:all` from this directory
# is the only thing that ships these functions.

# --- Required by every deploy script: `gcloud functions deploy --project=` ---
# The project the functions run in. This moved to `hector-golf` on 2026-09-14,
# when phase 4 of docs/plans/functions-migration.md deployed all four there with
# their keys mounted from Secret Manager.
#
# The four functions in `gen-lang-client-0537211409` are still up and still
# answering — phase 7 deletes them after a week with no traffic — so pointing
# this back there still works, and still deploys to the copy that is on its way
# out. Prefer `hector-golf`.
GCLOUD_PROJECT_ID=hector-golf

# --- Required by the three Gemini functions ---
# ExtractScorecardInformation, GeneratePlayerBiography, GeneratePlayerAvatar.
# Both are passed to the deployed function as --set-env-vars, so they are
# runtime configuration as well as deploy-time.
GOOGLE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key
# The bearer token callers present to those three functions. The site's own
# .env has to carry the same value — see astrosite/.env.sample.
ASTROSITE_API_KEY=your_backend_function_bearer_token

# --- Required by deploy:tournament-leaderboard ---
# app.hector.golf answers 401 without it. The function holds it server-side so
# that the public site never ships it.
HECTOR_APP_API_KEY=your_app_hector_golf_api_key

# --- Only for the GeneratePlayerAvatar CLI, not for any deploy ---
# src/cli/generate-player-avatar.ts calls a *deployed* function and needs its
# URL. Either set this outright, or leave it unset and let the CLI build the
# URL from FUNCTION_REGION and GCLOUD_PROJECT_ID above.
# GENERATE_PLAYER_AVATAR_URL=https://europe-north1-<project>.cloudfunctions.net/GeneratePlayerAvatar
FUNCTION_REGION=europe-north1
